[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Managed execution defaults and narrow CIL continuation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AOT-DEFER-001
TITLE: JIT default with explicit deferred native qualification
STATEMENT: >>>
Ordinary and qualified simulator benchmark invocations shall not select a Native
AOT job by default. Qualified managed execution expects four successful API/RAM
measurements. Preserve the previous eight-case native profile only behind an
explicit --include-native-aot opt-in combined with --qualified-baseline. Reject
missing, duplicated and null profile controls before starting tool work. Preserve
BenchmarkDotNet argument order and retain historical native evidence separately.
Verification: LauncherProfileTests and an actual four-case default JIT invocation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CIL-NARROW-001
TITLE: Explicit unchecked small-integer evaluation-stack conversions
STATEMENT: >>>
The scheduled UInt32/Int32/Boolean frontend shall accept conv.i1, conv.u1, conv.i2
and conv.u2 on its 32-bit evaluation stack. Truncate to eight or sixteen low bits
first, then sign-extend signed opcodes or zero-extend unsigned opcodes to 32 bits.
Keep one-instruction-per-edge scheduling, start-time argument capture and original
IL provenance. Compare all four raw-IL operations and a composed C# example with
actual CLR execution, an independent modular arithmetic oracle and generated HDL.
Verification: ScheduledNarrowConversionTests and narrow HDL replay.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CIL-NARROW-002
TITLE: Maintain conversion-profile rejection and local-proof boundaries
STATEMENT: >>>
Checked, 64-bit, floating and native-sized conversions, narrow locals/ports and
malformed stacks remain unsupported and shall report original method/IL context.
Native bit-vector checks of conversion cones shall retain real UNSAT/SAT results
and independently replay counterexamples, without describing local combinational
checks as a sequential-design proof. Retain finite campaign and coverage limits.
Verification: negative/malformed tests and NarrowConversionProofTests.
The narrow locals/ports restriction is superseded by CIL-STORAGE-001. Historical
evidence in the original continuation report remains scoped to that revision.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLS-SIGN-001
TITLE: Bounded explicit sign-extension values
STATEMENT: >>>
ScheduledValue.SignExtend shall preserve the source two's-complement bit pattern
by replicating its sign bit into a result at least as wide and at most 4096 bits.
Identity extension shall preserve the value object; narrowing and excessive widths
shall reject before lowering. Emit the existing typed Core SignExtend operation.
Verification: width/identity/boundary tests and independent native arithmetic miters.
<<<
